= The Hunger Strike

Republican prisoners in the Maze are refusing food. They want to be treated as political prisoners, not criminals: their own clothes, no prison work, free association. Their leader, Bobby Sands, has been elected to Parliament for Fermanagh and South Tyrone while starving himself.

- @refuse: "Crime is crime is crime. It is not political."
- @concede: Quietly grant most of the prisoners' demands.

@refuse
on-arrival: uup_relation += 5; right_dissent -= 3; thatcher_rating += 1; europe_relation -= 5; us_relation -= 5; partner_dissent -= 1 if govt_type = 2
achievement: hunger_strike

Sands dies after 66 days, and nine more hunger strikers follow him before the protest ends. Over 100,000 people attend his funeral. The IRA recruits as never before, but the government doesn't give way.

@concede
on-arrival: hunger_strike_conceded = 1; uup_relation -= 20; right_dissent += 12; thatcher_rating -= 4; partner_dissent += 4 if govt_type = 2; us_relation += 3

The prisoners are allowed their own clothes and given most of what they asked for. The strike ends without deaths. The Unionists and our own right accuse us of surrendering to terrorism.
